revision            0

description         \
    Containerize your development and continuous integration environments.

long_description    \
    Toast is a tool for doing work in containers. You define tasks in a YAML \
    file called a toastfile, and Toast runs them in a containerized \
    environment based on a Docker image of your choosing. What constitutes a \
    \"task\" is up to you: tasks can install system packages, build an \
    application, run a test suite, or even serve web pages. Tasks can depend \
    on other tasks, so Toast can be understood as a high-level containerized \
    build system.

